#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:9
msgid ""
"Allow (optional) named function parameters in parenthesized generic argument "
"lists, such as those of `Fn`, `FnMut`, `FnOnce`, `AsyncFn`, `AsyncFnMut`, "
"and `AsyncFnOnce`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:17
msgid ""
"Similar to named function pointer parameters, these names don't affect "
"rust's semantics."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:19
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:22
msgid "Benefit: Better documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:24
msgid ""
"This allows users to better document the meaning of parameters in "
"signatures. This is the primary benefit of this RFC."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:26
msgid ""
"For example, it is not immediately clear what the `String` and `usize` refer "
"to in the type of `log`, providing names like in the example above is much "
"clearer."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:35
msgid "The parameter names should also show up on rustdoc."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:37
msgid "Benefit: Better LSP hints"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:39
msgid ""
"When calling `log` in the body of `parse_my_data`, the LSP can provide the "
"function parameter names as \"inlay parameter name hints\": log(`data: "
"`\"Message\".to_string(), `priority: `1);"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:42
msgid ""
"This is a concrete advantage of this approach over using comments to do the "
"same thing, such as in:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:50
msgid "Benefit: Better consistency with `fn` pointers"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:52
msgid "Imagine if `parse_my_data` looked like this:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:60
msgid ""
"If due to new requirements the user decides that `impl Fn` suits the usecase "
"better, having to remove the parameter names is unintuitive. This RFC "
"removes this problem."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:63
msgid "Guide-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:66
msgid ""
"You can give names to parameters to the `Fn` trait and its friends to better "
"document the meaning of these parameters, to help people who call your "
"function. These names are optional and don't have any semantic meaning. "
"Named and unnamed parameters can be mixed, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:76
msgid "This same syntax also applies to trait bounds, for example:"
msgstr ""

