#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:153
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:156
msgid ""
"This makes the syntax of `impl Fn` and friends slightly more complicated"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:157
msgid ""
"This keeps the syntax of `impl Fn` and friends inconsistent with that of "
"functions in trait definitions, for the reasoning about this see  [reference "
"level explanation](#reference-level-explanation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:159
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:162
msgid ""
"This needs to be implemented in the language, it cannot be provided by a "
"macro or library as it affects syntactic sugar of the language itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:163
msgid ""
"This makes Rust code easier to read, as it adds better ways to document "
"function signatures."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:165
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr ""

