msgid "In TypeScript:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:178
msgid "In Kotlin:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:183
msgid "Unresolved questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:186
msgid ""
"Should duplicate parameter names be allowed in named fn trait arguments? "
"This is currently allowed for `fn` pointers and other functions without an "
"accompanying `Body`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:196
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:199
msgid ""
"We should figure out how this feature interacts with the \"named arguments\" "
"feature. One proposal is to mirror whatever solution we come up with for "
"function pointers. For example, if named arguments used the syntax `fn f(pub "
"a: T, pub b: U) -> R`, the function trait should be `Fn(pub a: T, pub b: U) -"
"> R`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3955-named-fn-trait-parameters.md:202
msgid ""
"Similarly, we should figure out how this feature interacts with the "
"\"defaulted arguments\" feature. Again, this should mirror function "
"pointers. For example, if default arguments used the syntax `fn(x: String, "
"y: i32 = 0)`, the function trait should be `Fn(x: String, y: i32 = 0)`."
msgstr ""
